I come out of the market.
There are heavy cloth bags in my hands.
It is very hot even in the morning.
I feel very tired.
I walk to the main road.
There are many autos on the road.
I go near an auto.
"I need to go to Kaloor," I tell the driver.
"How many rupees will it be to Kaloor?"
I ask.
"It will be eighty rupees," the driver replies.
I agree to that.
"Okay, let's go," I say.
First, I place the bags in the auto.
Then I climb in and sit in the auto.
The auto starts the journey to my flat.
I feel very relieved.
